{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788125034,"nonce":"J7MXjGz1xU7zxnz4ZiFhRSlxHtk=","message":"Open-question resolutions (worker, in-session on BORGES):\n\n**Default viewport + max:** around-mode default radius 12 (25x25), hard cap 60x60 per crop (CropRenderer.MaxSide, enforced with a bad-args error). A 25x25 crop with legend lands ~1.5-2.5KB — glance-compatible; bigger looks are explicit rect requests.\n\n**Glyphs for stacked/multi-cell things:** one thing per cell wins by rank (building \u003e item \u003e plant), and a multi-cell building renders its glyph in every occupied cell — coherent by construction since the glyph is a function of the def, not the cell. Stacking detail is the legend's job (each glyph lists the def labels it covered this crop, pipe-separated).\n\n**find-rect scoring:** v1 score = center distance from `near`, ascending — nothing cleverer until play data (4.3) shows what else matters (the rejected tally already reports WHY nearby space failed, which is the actionable half). Requirements: buildable (Heavy affordance + no edifice), walkable, roofed/unroofed, reachable-from:P.\n\n**Pawn rendering:** pawns always win the cell; glyph by allegiance — @ colonist, $ prisoner, ! hostile, g neutral/guest humanlike, d tame animal, w wild — and the legend appends actual names per glyph (capped 8), so a crop identifies WHO without per-pawn glyph churn.","files":null}]}